{"id":"HKF-032","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: binary model-selection variable beta_r (small vs large model per request) and binary 3D layer-to-UAV assignment alpha_{r,n,j}. Objective: maximize average normalized utility (1/R) sum(lambda_1Ar - lambda_2Lr). Constraints: per-UAV memory (11), computation (12), unique layer execution (13), binary variables (14). Solver: Genetic Algorithm (DMS, Algs. 1-2) with tournament selection, dual crossover, and capacity/distance-weighted mutation (x_n^t = f_n/d_{k,n}^t, P_n). Missing: GA population/generation/mutation values and lambda_1, lambda_2.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"III.C Problem Formulation","quote":"(βr ,αr,n,j )"},{"page":4,"section":"IV. ALGORITHM DESIGN","quote":"which is based on genetic algorithms [20]."},{"page":5,"section":"V.A Simulation Settings","quote":"we set the available memory for the Raspberry Pi Zero to 256MB."}],"note":""}
