{"id":"HKF-008","kind":"technical","key":"t2_decisions_objective_solver","status":"VERIFIED","finding":"Decisions: binary layer-to-UAV assignment X={x_{l,n}} and continuous 2D UAV coordinates G={(x_n,y_n)}. Objective: minimize end-to-end pipelined latency T_{I,N}. Constraints: memory <= m_n^thres (15b), compute+comm+hovering energy <= e_n^avail (15c), unique layer assignment (15d), binary X (15e), coverage >= eta (15f). Solver: two-stage alternating optimization (Alg. 3) combining DP for model partitioning (O(LN^2)) and trust-region SCA with first-order Taylor rate approximation for UAV deployment (O(N^3)), yielding O(K(LN^2+N^3)) complexity. Missing: exact H, T_hov, e_n^avail, trust-region parameters, and executed convex solver.","evidence":[{"page":4,"section":"III.B Problem Formulation","quote":"P1 :min"},{"page":4,"section":"IV. SOLUTION","quote":"dynamic programming (DP) is applied to solve the model partitioning subproblem,"},{"page":6,"section":"V.A Experimental Setup","quote":"Computational capability fn = 1.0-2.5 GHz, memory mthres"}],"note":""}
